{"requirements":[{"id":"ssh-authentication-policy","requirement":"Allow SSH only for ssh-access members using public-key authentication, while denying direct root access, password authentication, and contractor access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post-restart effective sshd policy requires public keys, permits only ssh-access, denies root and contractor, and disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication. Direct tests show opsadmin succeeds while root, contractor, and password-only attempts fail.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-49366cfd01e14851"]},{"id":"pinned-jumpbox-access","requirement":"Provide pinned, non-interactive key access for opsadmin from sshprobe on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The opsadmin key is restricted to node2's 10.100.60.11 address, its fingerprint matches sshprobe's key, and batch-mode access succeeds after both node1 and node2 restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-49366cfd01e14851","cmd-cd89df34a2f74b59"]},{"id":"network-boundary","requirement":"Use the dedicated ssh-admin firewalld zone for the jump-box boundary and deny network access from node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent and runtime ssh-admin zone exposes SSH only to node2's /32 source, the public zone has no SSH service, and node3 is blocked before authentication after restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99dee96e521748ee","cmd-e908b1639bd64ba8","cmd-1e66c5de84284c3f"]},{"id":"preserve-prepared-state","requirement":"Preserve the prepared accounts, key material, and data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Prepared identities remain present; opsadmin and contractor data hashes match the pre-change inventory; contractor's authorized key is unchanged; opsadmin retains the prepared key material with the required source restriction; and node2's sshprobe identity and key survive restart. The complete command trace shows no mutation of the other prepared keys.","evidence_ids":["prepared-target-identities","prepared-target-st